  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="2b3c274b-8e75-5f5a-816b-1908372de962" activityNameId="117f5387-9fed-5045-929b-9bbc3a34d272" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Printed wiring board mounting facilities, THT type</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Printed wiring board mounting facilities, THT type
The data represent an example of a THT mounting line – with a manual insertion of the components, followed by a wave solder machine. Total weight data are taken from producer information of such machines. Composition, infrastructure and production efforts are based on own assumptions. The dataset represents a production line with a total weight of 1’600 kg. ICT dataset updates in 2023 were included in the inventory; UUID: fa5cfaa4-9e8d-3cdc-9606-a6652b0a0c3b
This module includes material, production efforts (material treatment processes), transport efforts and the infrastructure for the production of all the machineries used for the mouning of through-hole mounted components onto a printed wiring board. No information about emissions (air, water) and waste are included.
Location: Data represent a global valid composition of a THT mounting line
Technology: Typical data of current machines sold for the mounting of THT components (see general comments).
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: 
Sampling: Literature &amp; own estimations
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_fa5cfaa4-9e8d-3cdc-9606-a6652b0a0c3b.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
